<title>RUSSIA: Russian January trade surplus widens to $2.1 bln.</title>
<headline>Russian January trade surplus widens to $2.1 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia recorded a January preliminary trade surplus of $2.1 billion, up from a $1.8-billion surplus in January 1996, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS:</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE    Jan 97     Jan 96     Jan 95</p>
<p>    exports			     4.8	  4.7	  4.5</p>
<p>    imports			     2.7	  2.8	  2.8</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +2.1	 +1.8	 +1.7</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE    Jan 97     Jan 96     Jan 95</p>
<p>    exports			     6.1	  6.0	  5.5</p>
<p>    imports			     3.8	  4.5	  3.7</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +2.3	 +1.5	 +1.8</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
